=== launch skill relevant lines ===
15:- **For Code OSS (VS Code dev build):** The repo must be built before launching. `./scripts/code.sh` runs the build automatically if needed, or set `VSCODE_SKIP_PRELAUNCH=1` to skip the compile step if you've already built.
41:# NOTE: unset ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE if running from a Claude Code terminal
42:unset ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE
43:./scripts/code.sh --remote-debugging-port=9224
82:The VS Code repository includes `scripts/code.sh` which launches Code OSS from source. It passes all arguments through to the Electron binary, so `--remote-debugging-port` works directly:
86:./scripts/code.sh --remote-debugging-port=9224
102:- Unset `ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE` before launching if it's set in your shell (e.g., in Claude Code terminals): `unset ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE && ./scripts/code.sh --remote-debugging-port=9224`
103:- Set `VSCODE_SKIP_PRELAUNCH=1` to skip the compile step if you've already built: `VSCODE_SKIP_PRELAUNCH=1 ./scripts/code.sh --remote-debugging-port=9224` (from the repo root)
104:- Code OSS uses the default user data directory. Unlike VS Code Insiders, you don't typically need `--user-data-dir` since there's usually only one Code OSS instance running.
105:- If you see "Sent env to running instance. Terminating..." it means Code OSS is already running and forwarded your args to the existing instance. Quit Code OSS and relaunch with the flag, or use `--user-data-dir=/tmp/code-oss-debug` to force a new instance.
113:./scripts/code.sh --agents --remote-debugging-port=9224
133:To debug a VS Code extension via npx @playwright/cli, launch VS Code Insiders with `--extensionDevelopmentPath` and `--remote-debugging-port`. Use `--user-data-dir` to avoid conflicting with an already-running instance.
143:  --remote-debugging-port=9223 \
144:  --user-data-dir=/tmp/vscode-ext-debug
157:- `--remote-debugging-port=9223` — enables CDP (use 9223 to avoid conflicts with other apps on 9222)
158:- `--user-data-dir=<path>` — uses a separate profile so it starts a new process instead of sending to an existing VS Code instance
160:**Without `--user-data-dir`**, VS Code detects the running instance, forwards the args to it, and exits immediately — you'll see "Sent env to running instance. Terminating..." and CDP never starts.
174:#    Normally you can skip a manual step here and let ./scripts/code.sh in step 3
184:./scripts/code.sh --remote-debugging-port=9224
321:- Make sure Code OSS was launched with `--remote-debugging-port=NNNN`

